        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7352080?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Removing documentation of the <code class=\"notranslate\">offline-enabled</code> manifest key, which was supported by Chrome in Manifest V2 (Firefox and Safari never supported this key). The feature was marked as deprecated in <a href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/25117\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/25117/hovercard\">WebExtensions - fix up all the tags except for apis</a> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1612323920\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/25117\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/25117/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/25117\">#25117</a>. Chrome ceased support for Manifest V2 in version 139.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #44817.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4919667433\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44817\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/44817/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44817\">#44817</a><br>\nRelating BCD changes in PR  <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4923775154\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/30080\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30080/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30080\">mdn/browser-compat-data#30080</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44823",
            "title": "Remove the `offline-enabled` manifest key docs",
            "date_modified": "2026-07-20T17:34:50.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-07-19T17:53:34.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "rebloor",
                "url": "https://github.com/rebloor"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7352080?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This change adds details to the content scripts page's limitation section on running scripts in <code class=\"notranslate\">about:</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">data:</code>, and <code class=\"notranslate\">blob:</code> pages. This is a follow-up that details the new behavior introduced with:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1475831\" rel=\"nofollow\">Bug 1475831</a> WebExtension: content scripts should be injected in data URL pages</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1897113\" rel=\"nofollow\">Bug 1897113</a> Content scripts should only run in blob:-URLs if match_origin_as_fallback is true</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1896669\" rel=\"nofollow\">Bug 1896669</a> \"Dark Background and Light Text\" add-on stops working</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1853411\" rel=\"nofollow\">Bug 1853411</a> Implement matchOriginAsFallback in the scripting.registerContentScripts API)</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Details of the match origins fallback settings were previously added in <a href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/34491#top\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/34491/hovercard\">Docs for content script injection into data URL pages</a> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2380904285\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/34491\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/34491/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/34491\">#34491</a>.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #34532.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2383145414\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/34532\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/34532/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/34532\">#34532</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44822",
            "title": "Issue 34532 additional content script limitations",
            "date_modified": "2026-07-20T15:15:55.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-07-19T16:49:23.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "rebloor",
                "url": "https://github.com/rebloor"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/237978098?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #44817.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4919667433\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44817\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/44817/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44817\">#44817</a>. Adds a note clarifying that offline_enabled is a Manifest V2-only key and has no effect in Manifest V3 (supported in Chrome 88+).</p>\n\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Adds a note to the <code class=\"notranslate\">offline_enabled</code> manifest key page clarifying that it is only applicable to Manifest V2, and has no effect in Manifest V3.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome deprecated <code class=\"notranslate\">offline_enabled</code> when it moved to Manifest V3 (generally supported since Chrome 88). The current page did not mention this, which could confuse readers still relying on this key. Adding a clear note prevents that confusion.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://developer.chrome.com/docs/extensions/mv2/manifest/offline-enabled\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.chrome.com/docs/extensions/mv2/manifest/offline-enabled</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://developer.chrome.com/docs/extensions/develop/migrate/manifest\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.chrome.com/docs/extensions/develop/migrate/manifest</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #44817.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4919667433\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44817\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/44817/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44817\">#44817</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44820",
            "title": "Add note about offline_enabled being unsupported in Manifest V3",
            "date_modified": "2026-07-20T17:01:19.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-07-19T05:09:10.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chigicherlachinmaya-arch",
                "url": "https://github.com/chigicherlachinmaya-arch"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/91409429?u=4e1f7b62160e72ba743c04565340fd30f04e290a&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #44780.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4916588237\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44780\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/44780/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44780\">#44780</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The HTMLImageElement.x and .y properties are available for all images, not just those with display: table-column. Removed the incorrect restriction from both property docs.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44818",
            "title": "fix: remove incorrect table-column restriction for HTMLImageElement.x and .y",
            "date_modified": "2026-07-20T18:02:39.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-07-18T19:19:50.000Z",
            "author": {
